# Protect private athlete information

Athlete and user data is private. That includes names, contact details, health, injuries, body measurements, workout history, and payment identity.

- Do not log, print, commit, or paste private athlete data into code, fixtures, docs, screenshots, or chat.
- Use synthetic data in examples and tests.
- Do not weaken authentication, authorization, or row-level access checks.
- When a change reads or writes personal data, confirm the existing security check still limits access to the authorized user.
- Do not expose secrets, tokens, or production credentials in the diff or the reply.
